@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.dxp.cloud.subscription"

Feature: OSB DXP Cloud Partner Subscription
	Testing automatic subscriptions to DXP Cloud Partners for customers on OSB accounts with DXP cloud subscriptions.

Setup:
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                          |
	* I assign the web user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	* I assign the web user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to the web role "Verified User"
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Name   | Dxppar - ${staticCompanyName} | |
	| Code   | DXPPARDXPPAR                  | |
	| Status | Active                        | |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" on the account "Dxppar - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Partner Manager |
	* I set the project details non abbreviated date method to true
	* I generate static start and end dates
	* I generate past static start and end dates
	* I generate static full non abbreviated start and end dates
	* I generate future static full non abbreviated start and end dates
	* I generate past static full non abbreviated start and end dates
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dxppar - ${staticCompanyName}" and the product "Service Partnership" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual               | false                    | |
	| Quantity                | 1                        | |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       | |
	| Status                  | Approved                 | |
	* I create an assigned team nested field for a team with the name "Dxppar - ${staticCompanyName}" assigned to the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}"
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Assigned Team Nested Field | ${staticAssignedTeamNestedField} | |
	| Code                       | DXCZENDXCZEN                     | |
	| Name                       | Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}    | |
	| Region                     | United States                    | |
	| Status                     | Active                           | |
	| Tier                       | T1                               | |
	* I assign the team with the name "Dxppar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	* I assign the team with the name "Dxppar - ${staticCompanyName}" on the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "DXP Cloud Subscription HA Production" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I create a product purchase for an account with the name "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" and the product "Limited Subscription" on koroneiki with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |   |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |   |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |   |
	| Product Field and Value | sizing                   | 1 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |   |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |   |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |   |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Limited Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	* I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Partner"
	* I wait for "1" minutes
	* the support organization with the code "DXCZENDXCZEN" should be part of the support site

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Dxppar - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the product consumptions on koroneiki made by the account "Dxppar - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                       |
	| Limited Subscription                 |
	| DXP Cloud Subscription HA Production |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Dxppar - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| DXP Production                       |
	| Limited Subscription                 |
	| DXP Cloud Subscription HA Production |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the following products
	| Service Partnership |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Dxppar - ${staticCompanyName}" for the following products
	| Service Partnership |
 	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
 	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Dxczen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Dxppar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| DXPPARDXPPAR |
	| DXCZENDXCZEN |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Limited Subscription"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| DXPPARDXPPAR |
	| DXCZENDXCZEN |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Dxczen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Dxppar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Dxczen - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Dxppar - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the user email addresses from DXP Cloud subscription list
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |

Scenario: Expire a cloud subscription and check partner status  
	Partner users providing services to an account with DXP Cloud subscriptions get subscribed and also do not get automatically unsubscribed when expiring the Dxp Cloud Subscription

	Given I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I manually add the user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to the DXP Cloud subscription list
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	Then the user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Cloud Subscription HA Production" to have the following values
	| End Date          | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual         | false                        | |
	| Start Date        | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status            | Approved                     | |
	And I update a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Limited Subscription" to have the following values
	| End Date          | ${staticPastEndDate}         | |
	| Original End Date | ${staticPastOriginalEndDate} | |
	| Perpetual         | false                        | |
	| Start Date        | ${staticPastStartDate}       | |
	| Status            | Approved                     | |
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	Then the user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud

Scenario: Remove a cloud subscription and check partner status  
	Partner users providing services to an account with DXP Cloud subscriptions get subscribed and also do not get automatically unsubscribed when removing the Dxp Cloud Subscription

	Given I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I manually add the user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to the DXP Cloud subscription list
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	Then the user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "DXP Cloud Subscription HA Production"
	And I delete a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Dxczen - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Limited Subscription"
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	Then the user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be subscribed on DXP cloud

Scenario: Check that a partner user does not get automatically added to the subscription list
	Partner users providing services to an account with DXP Cloud subscriptions do not get automatically subscribed to the Dxp Cloud Subscription

	Given I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I manually add the user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to the DXP Cloud subscription list
	And I wait for "1" minutes
	Then the user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud
	Then the user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be subscribed on DXP cloud

